  "query_preview": "..(Thursday night through Tuesday) \nIssued at 917 AM EDT WED MAY 27 2026\n\nA northeast CONUS upper trough should temporarily retreat retreat\nslightly to the northeast for Friday before it is re-energized by\nan upper low as we move into the weekend. This could allow deep\nmoisture to sneak northeastward, and there is a potential for\nprecip which makes it back into our area from the southwest,\nmainly Friday into Saturday. Once the trough strengthens again,\nmainly dry weather should make a comeback before the weekend is\nfinished. Yet another cold front could pass on Monday. The GFS\ntries to generate some light precip with this, but it looks like\navailable moisture would be limited. However, if the GFS  \npersists or the ECMWF were to join it, its possible a POP may \nneed to be introduced in later updates.",
